## 🤔 What makes this different from "chat with your PDF"?

Most AI document tools just answer questions. This one **takes actions**:

| Feature | Chat with PDF tools | This agent |
|---|---|---|
| Reads document content | ✅ | ✅ |
| Extracts structured fields | ❌ | ✅ |
| Checks against a budget | ❌ | ✅ |
| Logs entry to a database | ❌ | ✅ |
| Sends real alerts | ❌ | ✅ |
| Remembers spending history | ❌ | ✅ |
| Shows reasoning trace | ❌ | ✅ |
| Handles scanned PDFs (OCR) | ❌ | ✅ |

The agent uses **Gemini function calling** to decide which tools to use and in what order — it is not a hardcoded if/else chain. Every decision is visible in the live reasoning trace.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
document-action-agent/
│
├── app.py            →  Streamlit UI (browser interface + file upload)
├── agent.py          →  Gemini function-calling loop + reasoning trace
├── extraction.py     →  PDF text extraction with OCR fallback
├── tools.py          →  4 tools the agent can call:
│                           • check_against_budget
│                           • log_entry
│                           • send_alert
│                           • get_spending_summary
├── main.py           →  CLI entry point (alternative to UI)
│
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.example      →  API key template
├── budgets.json      →  Auto-generated on first run, editable in UI
└── expense_log.csv   →  Auto-generated, running log of all documents
```

### How the agent loop works

```
User uploads PDF
      ↓
extraction.py → pdfplumber (fast path)
              → pytesseract OCR (fallback for scanned PDFs)
      ↓
agent.py sends extracted text + available tools to Gemini 2.0 Flash
      ↓
Gemini reasons and calls tools in sequence:
  1. get_spending_summary()    → pulls full spending history
  2. check_against_budget()    → compares amount vs limit
  3. log_entry()               → writes to expense_log.csv
  4. send_alert()              → Slack webhook or console (if over budget)
      ↓
Gemini returns context-aware plain-English summary
      ↓
Streamlit UI displays: reasoning trace + summary + updated charts
```

